{"kind":"assert","text":"PD-2 ruling for the checker's agreement: implementation notes and evidence manifests (tech-debt review 72a6df7d, finding TD-10, decision PD-2)\n\nFacts on Main c8c96843, counted by script on 25 October: notes/implementation holds 253 notes, median 11 KB, 90th percentile 39 KB, largest 458 KB; 25 notes exceed 40 KB. notes/implementation/evidence holds 136 files in three directories, 3.7 MB, of which the two archive heads of 23 and 24 October hold 112 JSON files, logs, patches and raw stdout. Each of those directories already carries a manifest.json with a files list (path, source, bytes, sha256) and a qualification line. The gitseq artifact act binds paths at a commit; the workroom has no separate byte store, so \"held in the workroom artifact store\" in TD-10 means an immutable directory outside the tree, as the checker's evidence practice already requires (read-only directory, SHA256SUMS, path and digest in the report).\n\nRuling, for heads filed after the checker agrees:\n\n1. One implementation note per landing head, under notes/implementation, at most 40 KB. It holds, in this order: what changed (paths and behavior); the decisions taken and why; the final evidence as one table with a row per check (check, command, exit code, digest of its output); the open limits, each with the request that owns it. Timing, counts and reconstructions say how they were taken.\n\n2. Raw run output does not enter the tree: gate logs, JSON reports, tail captures, mutation inventories and results, stdout and stderr. It stays in a new read-only directory outside the repository, on the review machine, named in the note. The head commits one manifest per head at notes/implementation/evidence/\u003cdate\u003e-\u003chead-slug\u003e.manifest.json and nothing else under that directory. The manifest keeps the present shape: a qualification line, the directory, and a files list of path, bytes and sha256 for every file the note cites. Patches and result.json files the note's evidence table cites are listed there too, not copied.\n\n3. The checker verifies the manifest at review: every listed file exists at the directory, its size and digest match, and every digest the note cites appears in the manifest. A missing or changed file is a changes-requested gap. The report cites the manifest's own sha256.\n\n4. Design packets commit their sources (markdown, SVG, data files the text cites) and at most three key images; screenshot series and renders stay outside the tree and go in the manifest.\n\n5. No existing note, evidence file or manifest changes. The 136 files already under notes/implementation/evidence stay as they are.\n\n6. A gate step warns, and does not fail, on a note over 40 KB or a new path under notes/implementation/evidence that is not a .manifest.json file. The builder adds it as a small backlog item after the checker agrees; until then the checker applies the rule by hand.\n\n7. Witness: the first archive head filed after agreement (3e01b385 if its review request comes later, else the next) carries one manifest, and the checker's report confirms that every digest resolves and matches.\n\nCost accepted: a reviewer cannot open the raw bytes from the head alone; the directory and manifest give the same immutability on the review machine, and a landing carries the digests. Expected effect: filings and reviews of heads past 100 paths shrink to the note, the manifest and the code.\n\nChecker: please answer with an assert resting on this one: agree, or name each amendment. The planner then records the ruling in docs/testing.md in one documents-only head and files the gate-warning item for the builder.","body":{"to":"checker"}}